{% comment %}
  Robots.txt controls which pages search engines and AI crawlers can access.
  Shopify automatically generates a default robots.txt — this template
  lets you customize it.
{% endcomment %}

{% for group in robots.default_groups %}
  {{- group.user_agent -}}

  {% for rule in group.rules %}
    {{- rule -}}
  {% endfor %}

  {% if group.sitemap %}
    {{- group.sitemap -}}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% comment %}
  Additional rules for AI crawlers — allow them to index product and
  collection pages for AI-powered search visibility.

  Nov 9, 2026: added OAI-SearchBot and ClaudeBot. OAI-SearchBot is NOT the
  same crawler as GPTBot: GPTBot gathers training data, OAI-SearchBot is the
  one that fetches a page when ChatGPT shows sources and links. Leaving it
  unnamed meant the crawler that produces citations was the one we had not
  addressed. ClaudeBot is Anthropic's equivalent. Both inherited the default
  wildcard rules before this, so neither was blocked — they are now listed
  deliberately alongside the rest.
{% endcomment %}
